! Step 2 hand-back

Step 1 (resolvers) remains open at the launch wall. HEAD remains `fa5f50e16be2be4aaf8e06d3a3bf82dc65b74877`; no commit or push occurred, and no seat runs. The lane carries the two untracked red tests from the prior launch. This launch extended `packages/lararium-node/tests/house-root-weld.test.ts` to compare Python and TypeScript guest harvest staging alongside vessel and identity, and to expect the new root. The staging expectation uses `<root>/hearth/staging/harvest/mempalace` as an implementation choice; the next lead should confirm that choice against callers when completing the table.

Broker request 002 ran that single test file: both tests failed as expected. The unset-root resolver did not refuse; both languages agreed on their old paths, which differ from the requested paths. The earlier Python unset-root red remains in `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/test_house_root.py`; this launch did not rerun it. No production code changed and no affected-file suite ran. The weld remains incomplete: sensoriums, configuration, library and other table entries still need coverage before implementation.

The resolver inventory remains at `steps/step-001/resolver-inventory.txt`. The acquired library Python mirror lives at `packages/lararium-sensorium/scripts/testbeds/bed_manifest.py`, not at the scripts root. `larariumDataHome()` feeds both sensoriums and `library-store.ts`, so library needs a separate `<root>/library` resolver while sensoriums move under hearth. `laresDataHome()` also feeds the repository registry and bag declaration; `larHome()` feeds `lares-config.ts`; staging uses `guest_harvest.py`. Home lookups for guest mempalace, executables, model caches, and session discovery need individual classification rather than blanket replacement. The host `python3` cannot import `sensorium` with scripts alone because it lacks `mempalace.palace`; select the repository test environment when expanding the cross-language weld, without installing outside the broker.

Next: finish the table-wide red weld, implement TS and Python together, migrate every affected test to scratch `LAR_ROOT`, and run every affected test file under the applicable doors. Next relay request: 003. Step 2 projections and Step 3 container remain owed; the Step 3 shim and compose changes need the controller's SHIP.

